NNAAMMEE
     yyppwwhhiicchh — return hostname of YP server or map master

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     yyppwwhhiicchh [--tt] [--dd _d_o_m_a_i_n] [[--hh] _h_o_s_t]
     yyppwwhhiicchh [--tt] [--dd _d_o_m_a_i_n] [--hh _h_o_s_t] --mm [_m_n_a_m_e]
     yyppwwhhiicchh --xx

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     yyppwwhhiicchh tells which YP server supplies YP services to a client, or which
     is the master for a map.  If invoked without arguments, it gives the YP
     server for the local machine.  If _h_o_s_t is specified, that machine is
     queried to find out which YP server it is using.

     The options are as follows:

     --dd _d_o_m_a_i_n
             Specify a domain other than the default domain.

     --hh _h_o_s_t
             Specify which host to query.

     --mm [_m_n_a_m_e]
             Find the master YP server for the named map.  The _h_o_s_t to query,
             if non-default, must be specified using the --hh option.  _m_n_a_m_e can
             be a map name or nickname.  If _m_n_a_m_e is omitted, yyppwwhhiicchh will
             produce a list of available maps.

     --tt      Inhibit translation of map nicknames to their corresponding map
             names.

     --xx      Display the map nickname table.

